Renders each frame as late as it can and still make the next vblank, so
a client's commit that comes after the last vblank is shown at the next
one rather than a refresh later. The time left for rendering adapts to
the vblanks it misses. Upstream's niri-wm/niri#4692 by Liam Dyer, commit
d83adcab41c1560b3d23d49d7b6c0533ec799d08, made on niri 26.04 and the
patches before it here.

Unlike upstream, it's off unless NIRI_RENDER_DEADLINE=1 is in niri's
environment as it starts, rather than on unless debug's
disable-render-deadline says otherwise, so it adds no setting to niri's
config: a config written for this niri still parses in one without it.
render-deadline-action.patch turns it on and off while niri runs.

